WEBVTT

00:00:02.109 --> 00:00:05.279
Once, when many planets
intermingled and

00:00:05.613 --> 00:00:08.716
the boundary between man
and god was vague...

00:00:09.316 --> 00:00:14.221
There was a tale of a particular family.
A tale of love and rebirth.

00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:27.167
Sometimes I think things over.
It helps to cheer me up.

00:00:34.942 --> 00:00:37.678
K'Yy O U S O UG I G A

00:00:40.848 --> 00:00:44.552
This place has always
meant everything to me.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.857
It rains so beautifully here.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:55.296
I can dance like the wind.

00:00:57.798 --> 00:01:00.801
Even now, I'm having fun.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.640
I have a better sense of
rhythm than you'd think.

00:01:07.141 --> 00:01:12.313
It felt as though every time
I heard a certain someone's voice,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:22.723
I would think back to how
I grew up surrounded by laughter.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:28.762
Yes, anywhere would have
done as a place to call home.

00:01:28.762 --> 00:01:34.301
Farewell, sunshine!
The night rises up invitingly.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:39.573
It's okay, this world moves
in a way that will connect us.

00:01:39.807 --> 00:01:46.280
So that we can all smile
together once again.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:53.387
"True to thy station"

00:01:54.355 --> 00:01:57.358
“All people must remain true to their station in life. A monk must act as a monk should act, and a common person the same. The emperor must
act in accordance with his station, and so must his retainers. Anyone who does not act in accordance with his station, therefore, is evil.”

00:01:57.358 --> 00:02:01.428
So saith Priest Myoue of Toganoo.

00:02:01.428 --> 00:02:04.632
| do not seek salvation in the next life.

00:02:05.633 --> 00:02:10.004
| merely strive to be true
to my station in this life.

00:02:48.976 --> 00:02:49.777
Father...

00:02:51.078 --> 00:02:52.046
Mother...

00:03:17.871 --> 00:03:22.342
The Worries, Beginning,
and Ending of the Young Third Son

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.324
He's got a weird face.

00:03:37.458 --> 00:03:38.425
It's ugly.

00:03:38.692 --> 00:03:39.827
He's drooling! Gross!

00:03:39.827 --> 00:03:42.296
Gah! What are you guys doing here?

00:03:42.296 --> 00:03:43.731
What do you mean,
what are we doing here?

00:03:45.766 --> 00:03:47.434
Oh, you're up?

00:03:51.071 --> 00:03:52.873
Let's eat!

00:03:53.741 --> 00:03:55.375
Enjoy.

00:03:57.244 --> 00:03:57.845
Why?

00:03:59.546 --> 00:04:03.250
We told you to make breakfast first
if you're gonna be gone overnight!

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:04.885
They got hungry.

00:04:04.885 --> 00:04:05.719
Yum!

00:04:06.453 --> 00:04:08.355
Maybe we'll come back tomorrow.

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.458
Chapter 13: The Present
(8)/ Priest Myoue A

00:04:18.499 --> 00:04:19.133
Hey!

00:04:19.399 --> 00:04:20.634
| was going to get that!

00:04:21.368 --> 00:04:22.770
And give me my money back!

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:24.037
I'm not buying you a drink!

00:04:24.338 --> 00:04:24.838
Hey!

00:04:25.339 --> 00:04:26.039
Listen to me!

00:04:26.406 --> 00:04:27.174
Hey!

00:04:28.509 --> 00:04:29.143
Hey!

00:04:35.382 --> 00:04:36.717
I'll get you next time...

00:04:57.404 --> 00:04:58.639
I'll skip today.

00:05:00.674 --> 00:05:01.575
This is awful!

00:05:08.649 --> 00:05:12.085
Is it worth it to get so worked
up over a can of soda?

00:05:13.453 --> 00:05:16.523
And what's so important
that our little brother

00:05:16.523 --> 00:05:18.158
must skip the council meeting?

00:05:19.993 --> 00:05:23.497
He gets like this whenever this
time of year comes around.

00:05:24.832 --> 00:05:27.134
The train was empty again this year.

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:28.769
That's why.

00:05:29.102 --> 00:05:32.005
He doesn't want us to
see how depressed he is.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:36.910
He gets his hopes up for no reason,
and then thinks he's been betrayed.

00:05:37.377 --> 00:05:38.579
You're quite harsh.

00:05:38.745 --> 00:05:42.883
Well, he acts like he's
the only one who's hurt!

00:05:43.717 --> 00:05:45.419
It's the same for us!

00:05:46.119 --> 00:05:50.757
Well, not exactly the same,
which makes me even more mad.

00:05:51.358 --> 00:05:57.164
The king has yet to return,
and the old days are gone forever.

00:05:58.332 --> 00:06:01.235
Come to think of it,
there was a story I once heard.

00:06:03.203 --> 00:06:06.273
About a dog waiting faithfully
for his master to return.

00:06:08.141 --> 00:06:11.612
The dog stands in the same
spot, forever waiting.

00:06:12.512 --> 00:06:14.915
But his master is long dead.

00:06:15.649 --> 00:06:18.752
The dog doesn't know that,
so he waits and waits and waits.

00:06:19.219 --> 00:06:24.124
At long last, he finally tires
of waiting, and dies.

00:06:25.692 --> 00:06:26.760
Tragic, right?

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:28.629
Doesn't it make you want to cry?

00:06:29.529 --> 00:06:31.498
Did the dog have no legs?

00:06:31.498 --> 00:06:32.799
No bark to call his master?

00:06:32.799 --> 00:06:33.867
No ears to listen?

00:06:34.368 --> 00:06:35.602
If he did?

00:06:35.869 --> 00:06:37.204
Then the dog was a fool.

00:06:37.704 --> 00:06:38.939
Why do you say so?

00:06:39.806 --> 00:06:42.342
His master never told him to die, right?

00:06:42.576 --> 00:06:45.812
The Loyal Dog Ha***ko Would his master have
been happy that he died waiting for him?

00:06:46.079 --> 00:06:46.947
| see.

00:06:47.214 --> 00:06:49.116
An opinion true to your personality.

00:06:49.549 --> 00:06:52.219
| have my own thoughts on this tale.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:56.924
Was the dog's goal truly
to wait for his master?

00:06:57.891 --> 00:06:59.760
If waiting was his only goal,

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.063
wouldn't he have acted differently?

00:07:04.631 --> 00:07:10.904
But what if the dog's goal
was to die exactly as he did?

00:07:13.073 --> 00:07:13.974
Get to the point!

00:07:14.241 --> 00:07:16.743
Who cares how the dog felt?

00:07:16.944 --> 00:07:17.978
How scary.

00:07:18.245 --> 00:07:19.613
How terrifying indeed.

00:07:31.591 --> 00:07:32.359
Myoue!

00:07:33.327 --> 00:07:34.294
Myoue!

00:07:35.395 --> 00:07:35.963
Myoue!

00:07:36.697 --> 00:07:37.264
Hey.

00:07:37.798 --> 00:07:38.532
Hey, there.

00:07:39.333 --> 00:07:40.467
Got rid of your stuff?

00:07:40.767 --> 00:07:41.335
Yeah.

00:07:41.835 --> 00:07:42.402
You?

00:07:43.937 --> 00:07:44.404
Yup.

00:07:45.339 --> 00:07:46.340
You don't need that?

00:07:46.673 --> 00:07:48.041
That's why I'm getting rid of it.

00:07:48.809 --> 00:07:50.711
It's fine, I'll buy some new stuff.

00:07:51.244 --> 00:07:53.146
I'm jealous.

00:07:54.815 --> 00:07:56.316
Thought I might try soccer.

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.086
Koto's really good.

00:07:59.353 --> 00:08:00.220
Did you know that?

00:08:00.921 --> 00:08:01.755
Nope.

00:08:08.395 --> 00:08:09.229
Myoue!

00:08:11.999 --> 00:08:13.900
What are you doing here?

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:14.868
Dodgeball.

00:08:14.868 --> 00:08:16.003
Can't you tell?

00:08:17.104 --> 00:08:18.672
Say we're asking people for leads!

00:08:18.672 --> 00:08:20.874
We don't want him to think we're slacking.

00:08:21.575 --> 00:08:23.377
Searching for leads!

00:08:23.744 --> 00:08:25.579
You're just playing.

00:08:27.247 --> 00:08:28.315
Are you okay?

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:31.118
Is he dead?

00:08:31.118 --> 00:08:32.052
Is Myoue dead?

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:39.159
Things are really crazy
in the outside world. It's fun!

00:08:39.393 --> 00:08:40.427
| can't believe it!

00:08:41.428 --> 00:08:42.929
She's so weird, isn't she?

00:08:42.929 --> 00:08:44.631
Koto's always like this.

00:08:44.965 --> 00:08:46.700
| know she's weird.

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:47.834
It's true!

00:08:48.068 --> 00:08:49.536
I'll take you there sometime!

00:08:51.705 --> 00:08:52.339
Outside!

00:08:52.739 --> 00:08:53.907
I'll take you someday.

00:08:56.343 --> 00:08:57.177
But...

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:01.581
| promise.

00:09:03.717 --> 00:09:04.985
| look forward to it!

00:09:05.519 --> 00:09:06.186
Yay!

00:09:07.621 --> 00:09:08.989
Don't be irresponsible.

00:09:10.824 --> 00:09:14.628
You talk big for someone who
came here and can't leave.

00:09:15.629 --> 00:09:17.931
If you spend every day playing around,

00:09:18.231 --> 00:09:20.300
will something good just happen one day?

00:09:20.567 --> 00:09:24.571
Or do you just like this place so much,
you never want to leave?

00:09:25.172 --> 00:09:26.606
Myoue, what's wrong?

00:09:38.218 --> 00:09:40.320
| get pissed off whenever I look at you.

00:09:41.088 --> 00:09:42.823
You're stupid, selfish brats!

00:09:43.657 --> 00:09:45.892
| get stuck with the short
end of the stick every time!

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:53.200
Everybody gets in my way...

00:09:54.134 --> 00:09:56.503
Just get away from me already!

00:10:02.375 --> 00:10:03.076
Myoue?

00:10:06.012 --> 00:10:08.014
Ky OuUSsS O UGI G A

00:10:08.014 --> 00:10:09.483
Chapter 14: The Present
(9)/ Priest Myoue B

00:10:14.321 --> 00:10:15.689
Let me stay here tonight!

00:10:20.093 --> 00:10:22.796
Sorry for just showing up
like this, Miss Girlfriend.

00:10:22.996 --> 00:10:24.564
Myoue's like...

00:10:24.965 --> 00:10:27.434
| don't know what his deal is.

00:10:28.635 --> 00:10:31.805
So you came here to piss him off?

00:10:32.472 --> 00:10:34.708
Bringing a ton of food with you.

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:38.411
This is good!

00:10:39.279 --> 00:10:41.047
You're an interesting girl, Koto.

00:10:41.615 --> 00:10:44.918
You're the only one who can
get Myoue all mad like that.

00:10:44.918 --> 00:10:47.521
He's always mad.

00:10:47.888 --> 00:10:49.823
Maybe so.

00:10:52.792 --> 00:10:53.860
This really is good.

00:10:58.532 --> 00:11:01.334
He's mad all the time, sure.

00:11:01.735 --> 00:11:04.104
But back there, it was like...

00:11:09.843 --> 00:11:12.279
Did he really get mad at me?

00:11:14.347 --> 00:11:15.749
| don't know...

00:11:17.784 --> 00:11:19.619
| feel like I'm being wrongly punished.

00:11:21.621 --> 00:11:25.158
It's actually been quite a long
time since he's gotten mad.

00:11:26.393 --> 00:11:28.995
It felt like he'd given up.

00:11:31.431 --> 00:11:33.600
He's been lazing around for a long time.

00:11:35.402 --> 00:11:36.770
I'm glad you came.

00:11:40.574 --> 00:11:43.076
Try to save Myoue, okay, Koto?

00:11:49.416 --> 00:11:50.984
What are you talking about?

00:11:52.485 --> 00:11:53.253
Please.

00:11:55.755 --> 00:11:58.058
I'm the one who needs saving.

00:11:58.558 --> 00:11:59.726
You'll be fine!

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:03.129
You're pretty irresponsible,
Miss Girlfriend.

00:12:03.129 --> 00:12:05.398
Now, what to do about dinner...

00:12:06.032 --> 00:12:07.033
What do you want to eat?

00:12:07.267 --> 00:12:08.201
Meat or something!

00:12:08.501 --> 00:12:09.102
Or something?

00:12:09.502 --> 00:12:09.970
Yup!

00:13:03.123 --> 00:13:06.726
I'm sorry for forcing you to go
along with my little game for so long.

00:13:13.366 --> 00:13:15.635
This is the last selfish
request I'll make of you.

00:13:17.871 --> 00:13:20.240
| entrust the mantle of
"Priest Myoue™" to you.

00:13:25.779 --> 00:13:27.447
Watch the place while I'm gone, okay?

00:13:28.982 --> 00:13:30.383
I'll come back someday.

00:13:30.684 --> 00:13:33.887
And I'll bring with me the
beginning and the end.

00:13:35.722 --> 00:13:36.656
| promise.

00:13:38.058 --> 00:13:40.293
Wait for me, okay? Myoue...

00:14:21.935 --> 00:14:23.269
| know.

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:32.579
So now it's your turn, huh?

00:14:34.247 --> 00:14:35.315
Is she still here?

00:14:43.523 --> 00:14:46.326
You're travelling the wrong way.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:49.295
So young a child ought to
know which way she's going,

00:14:49.295 --> 00:14:51.164
even if she doesn't
know her own name!

00:14:51.331 --> 00:14:53.032
She'll have to go back here as luggage.

00:14:53.032 --> 00:14:56.035
She must be labeled
"Lass, with care," you know—

00:14:56.035 --> 00:14:59.339
You're travelling the wrong way.

00:14:59.706 --> 00:15:03.176
Never mind what they all say, my dear,

00:15:04.411 --> 00:15:08.982
but take a return-ticket
every time the train stops.

00:15:18.658 --> 00:15:22.095
Surely she's not on the train, is she?

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:23.897
Right?

00:15:32.505 --> 00:15:34.307
What's up, Inuyama-san?

00:15:34.307 --> 00:15:35.508
What are you doing here?

00:15:35.708 --> 00:15:37.744
Are you walking Myoue?

00:15:38.178 --> 00:15:39.312
Just kidding.

00:15:42.182 --> 00:15:43.216
It was just a joke.

00:15:43.216 --> 00:15:44.784
Don't get mad, Myoue.

00:15:45.151 --> 00:15:46.653
Waiting for a girl?

00:15:46.653 --> 00:15:47.487
Idiot.

00:15:48.688 --> 00:15:50.857
What about you?
Why are you here?

00:15:51.291 --> 00:15:53.626
Just trying to get a feel for the place.

00:15:54.394 --> 00:15:55.662
But I'm going home.

00:15:57.897 --> 00:16:01.935
Inuyama-san, did you come to get me?

00:16:02.368 --> 00:16:03.636
That's so nice.

00:16:03.837 --> 00:16:05.004
Thank you.

00:16:07.841 --> 00:16:09.242
Whaaaaat?

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:11.177
Nothing.

00:16:23.156 --> 00:16:24.123
Have you eaten?

00:16:26.993 --> 00:16:28.995
Ky OuUSsS O UGI G A

00:16:28.995 --> 00:16:30.530
Chapter 15: The
Present (10)/ The Two

00:16:34.334 --> 00:16:35.735
What's for dinner?

00:16:35.935 --> 00:16:36.870
Fish.

00:16:37.103 --> 00:16:39.239
What? Let's have real meat instead!

00:16:39.239 --> 00:16:43.009
Too fast! Too fast! Too fast!

00:16:44.077 --> 00:16:45.345
Want me to drive?

00:16:45.645 --> 00:16:46.279
No.

00:16:46.579 --> 00:16:48.848
Come on, just for a little!

00:16:48.848 --> 00:16:49.883
I - said, " , nO"'

00:16:49.883 --> 00:16:58.458
Invincible!! Bishamaru Passionate fighting spirit and punches! An
action-adventure film that will make you hold your breath in suspense!!

00:16:58.458 --> 00:16:59.225
Hey, hey.

00:16:59.559 --> 00:17:01.160
Would you just shut up?

00:17:12.605 --> 00:17:14.107
What is your problem?

00:17:14.674 --> 00:17:16.843
You said to shut up.

00:17:18.845 --> 00:17:20.046
What is this place?

00:17:20.046 --> 00:17:22.115
Almost everything's sold out.

00:18:07.727 --> 00:18:08.995
Feels kind of sad...

00:18:12.665 --> 00:18:13.566
Yeah.

00:18:32.251 --> 00:18:36.823
So you didn't think of
riding that home?

00:18:37.523 --> 00:18:38.691
Oh!

00:18:39.258 --> 00:18:41.160
It never occurred to me!

00:18:42.128 --> 00:18:43.863
You're smart, Myoue.

00:18:44.063 --> 00:18:44.497
Hey.

00:18:45.665 --> 00:18:47.166
I'll try it sometime.

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:48.801
Not now.

00:18:49.335 --> 00:18:50.503
I've got something to do.

00:18:51.471 --> 00:18:52.305
| see.

00:18:53.539 --> 00:18:55.642
Canlgo home?

00:18:55.642 --> 00:18:56.209
No.

00:18:56.743 --> 00:18:58.244
You can go on your own, right?

00:18:58.244 --> 00:18:59.512
It's just a no-go zone.

00:18:59.712 --> 00:19:00.313
No!

00:19:00.847 --> 00:19:03.116
If you don't come with me,
I'll start smashing stuff.

00:19:04.584 --> 00:19:06.119
A and Un are waiting.

00:19:06.486 --> 00:19:08.421
| promised to go get them.

00:19:11.524 --> 00:19:13.292
Myoue!

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:15.294
Right, right.

00:19:18.798 --> 00:19:19.766
| won't smash stuff.

00:19:20.033 --> 00:19:21.300
Better believe you won't.

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:28.374
| really love A and Un a lot.

00:19:28.908 --> 00:19:32.845
They're the first...
relatives... I ever had?

00:19:33.579 --> 00:19:35.415
Something like a family.

00:19:38.484 --> 00:19:40.653
You don't care if they're
not human like you?

00:19:40.953 --> 00:19:41.454
Nope!

00:19:42.455 --> 00:19:45.758
Do normal people use their
"family" as foot soldiers?

00:19:47.694 --> 00:19:50.763
Couldn't you come up with
better names for them?

00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:51.364
Nope.

00:19:52.198 --> 00:19:54.267
Like Tarou and Jirou or something.

00:19:55.702 --> 00:19:57.470
Those sound like old man names.

00:19:59.739 --> 00:20:01.741
They do not!

00:20:03.776 --> 00:20:05.178
The names they have are cool!

00:20:06.379 --> 00:20:11.584
A and Un mean "the beginning
and the end," I heard.

00:20:38.945 --> 00:20:43.116
Uh... well... like...

00:20:47.019 --> 00:20:48.688
| getit, I guess.

00:20:56.262 --> 00:20:58.131
Slap!

00:20:58.431 --> 00:20:59.365
Ow!

00:21:00.199 --> 00:21:01.501
You were wide open!

00:21:01.501 --> 00:21:02.368
You little...

00:21:02.368 --> 00:21:03.870
Wait, Koto!

00:21:13.513 --> 00:21:14.580
Wait!

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.149
Let me punch you!

00:21:16.149 --> 00:21:17.950
Dummy, dummy!

00:21:19.218 --> 00:21:21.420
You little...

00:21:29.562 --> 00:21:31.197
What was that for?!

00:21:47.446 --> 00:21:48.080
What?

00:21:49.415 --> 00:21:53.753
| think the rabbit you're
looking for is our mother.

00:21:54.654 --> 00:21:57.290
I'll help you find her.

00:22:48.107 --> 00:22:50.576
Let's make him our son.

00:22:53.813 --> 00:22:55.581
What happened?

00:22:56.482 --> 00:22:57.516
| found him.

00:23:03.623 --> 00:23:06.525
And in exchange, you can help me.

00:23:09.629 --> 00:23:12.265
There's a place it's about time I went to.

00:23:33.819 --> 00:23:35.421
When you find our mother...

00:23:36.555 --> 00:23:38.457
| want you to kill me.

00:23:47.199 --> 00:23:53.606
I'd even cut things off, (Ouch!)
to prove the fact I exist.

00:23:55.441 --> 00:24:01.547
Though eternal lies surround me,
they're my safety line.

00:24:03.349 --> 00:24:09.956
"Wanna take you high?"
The galaxy shakes. You smile.

00:24:11.524 --> 00:24:17.997
I want to touch you. I don't want
to hear that it's forbidden.

00:24:19.799 --> 00:24:23.469
Moved to emotion by arguments,
| cast aside reason.

00:24:23.469 --> 00:24:28.574
I enter a game of risk that's
devoid of reason.

00:24:31.844 --> 00:24:36.615
It's resplendent with rare pain.

00:24:40.052 --> 00:24:45.124
Mistaking the real for the unreal.

